// Rule: [T1484.001] Payload Ransomware - Domain Root GPO Change
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1484.001
// Classification: Validation query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Sentinel / Log Analytics
// Required telemetry: SecurityEvent
// Purpose: Validates collection and raw representation of Active Directory object creation and modification events before detecting groupPolicyContainer creation or domain root gPLink...
// Logic: Evaluate SecurityEvent for domain root gpo change using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in SecurityEvent; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: Important: a returned row is not proof of malicious GPO activity or PAYLOAD attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// PAYLOAD ransomware - Active Directory GPO change telemetry validation
// Classification: Validation query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Platform: Microsoft Sentinel / Log Analytics
// Required connector: Windows Security Events via AMA
// Prerequisites: Audit Directory Service Changes (Success), appropriate SACLs,
//                and collection of Event IDs 5136 and 5137 from every domain controller.
// Purpose: verify ingestion, actor attribution, and raw event representation before
//          designing a rule for groupPolicyContainer creation or domain-root gPLink changes.
// Important: a returned row is not proof of malicious GPO activity or PAYLOAD attribution.
//            EventData must be inspected to confirm ObjectDN, ObjectClass,
//            AttributeLDAPDisplayName, Value, and OperationType population.

SecurityEvent
| where EventSourceName == "Microsoft-Windows-Security-Auditing"
| where EventID in (5136, 5137)
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, EventID, Activity,
          SubjectAccount, SubjectUserName, SubjectDomainName,
          SubjectUserSid, SubjectLogonId, EventData
| order by TimeGenerated desc
